 "notes": "2026 is the last season of the 2023-2026 CONMEBOL rights cycle. Spanish-speaking South America, Mexico, Central America and the Caribbean: Disney (ESPN linear channels + Disney+ Premium, formerly Star+) holds all matches; Paramount holds a free-to-air package (Telefe in Argentina, Chilevision in Chile, plus Pluto TV). In Argentina, Fox Sports (basic cable) carries matches alongside Disney+ Premium in 2026 match listings; ESPN is not listed there. Brazil: Globo (free-to-air TV Globo + GE TV on YouTube), ESPN/Disney+ (main pay package) and Paramount+ (streaming, exclusive group-stage games). USA/Canada: beIN SPORTS (2023-2026). No official CONMEBOL per-country broadcaster list could be retrieved; per-country entries rely on 2026 news/match guides. Not covered for lack of sources: UK, most of Europe (except Spain and Portugal), Africa, Asia, Middle East. Future context: from 2027 Globo/ESPN keep Brazil rights, ESPN/Disney+ renewed for Latin America to 2030, and Univision/TUDN takes the US from 2027 (per Wikipedia).",
